sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as User
  participant W as Web app
  participant G as Gateway
  participant I as Identity
  participant DB as identity_db
  U->>W: email + password
  W->>G: POST /api/v1/auth/login
  G->>I: forward (public path, rate limited)
  I->>DB: load user, check status and lockout
  I->>I: BCrypt check
  alt wrong password
    I->>DB: failed_login_attempts + 1 (lock after the limit)
    I-->>W: 401 INVALID_CREDENTIALS
  else MFA is active (always for admins)
    I->>DB: insert mfa_challenges (hashed token, 5 min)
    I-->>W: 200 status MFA_REQUIRED + mfaToken
    U->>W: 6-digit code from authenticator app
    W->>G: POST /api/v1/auth/mfa/verify
    G->>I: forward
    I->>I: TOTP check, reject a reused time step
    I->>DB: consume challenge, insert refresh_tokens (mfa_verified = true)
    I-->>W: access token (RS256, 15 min, amr = [pwd, mfa]) + refresh token
  else no MFA
    I->>DB: insert refresh_tokens
    I-->>W: status AUTHENTICATED, access token (amr = [pwd]) + refresh token
  end
  Note over W,I: Later, POST /auth/refresh rotates the refresh token. Reusing an old one revokes the whole family.
